# Integer math: the clean uniform interface. The host-backed operations (absolute, minimum, maximum, power, sign, square-root) delegate to the per-backend native implementation in its own file (`native/<env>/math`). Operations with no host primitive (clamp, greatest-common-divisor, factorial) compose from the interface in pure Seed. `number` is the platform integer (i64 / Int / Long), so round-down / round-up / round are the identity.

load @term/seed/code/native/math
  find abs
  find min
  find max
  find pow
  find signum
  find sqrt

task absolute
  take value, like number
  like number
  send back
    call abs
      read value

task minimum
  take a, like number
  take b, like number
  like number
  send back
    call min
      read a
      read b

task maximum
  take a, like number
  take b, like number
  like number
  send back
    call max
      read a
      read b

task power
  take base, like number
  take exponent, like number
  like number
  send back
    call pow
      read base
      read exponent

task sign
  take value, like number
  like number
  send back
    call signum
      read value

task square-root
  take value, like number
  like number
  send back
    call sqrt
      read value

task round-down
  take value, like number
  like number
  send back
    read value

task round-up
  take value, like number
  like number
  send back
    read value

task round
  take value, like number
  like number
  send back
    read value

task clamp
  take value, like number
  take low, like number
  take high, like number
  like number
  send back
    call minimum
      call maximum
        read value
        read low
      read high

task greatest-common-divisor
  take a, like number
  take b, like number
  like number
  save x, read a
  save y, read b
  walk test
    hook test
      call is-above
        read y
        code 0
    hook step
      save temp, read y
      save y
        call modulo
          read x
          read y
      save x, read temp
  send back, read x

task factorial
  take n, like number
  like number
  save result, code 1
  save count, code 1
  walk test
    hook test
      call is-maximum
        read count
        read n
    hook step
      save result
        call multiply
          read result
          read count
      save count
        call add
          read count
          code 1
  send back, read result
